{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
  "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in Case 08-1119, Milavetz, Gallop & Milavetz v. United States and United States v. Milavetz."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Milavetz, Gallop & Milavetz, P.A., et al.",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRUNSTAD: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Section 526(a)(4) is unconstitutional because it proscribes truthful information about entirely lawful activity, it whipsaws the attorneys who are trying to apply it, it creates an impossible situation for them, and it harms the client."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: If it were confined to unlawful activity and narrowly drawn, do you concede that such a statute would be constitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem, Justice Breyer, is that I think when Your Honor was quoting from section 101(4A), Your Honor took out a whole lot of information that goes between the word \"bankruptcy assistance\" and \"legal representation.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How is it any different from including lawyers within the category \"debt collectors,\" which lawyers objected to in this Court unsuccessfully?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it a normal facial invalidity? Is it an overbreadth invalidity? Is it an as-applied challenge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We brought this lawsuit as a declaratory judgment action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A debt relief agency is any person who provides specified services to specified clients for pay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "An attorney is a person, a defined term under the Bankruptcy Code, and the Petitioners have affirmatively alleged in their complaint that they provide bankruptcy assistance to assisted persons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0001-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "An attorney -- sorry. A client who incurs additional debt intending to defraud the creditor may not be able to obtain a discharge of that debt and indeed may not be able to obtain a discharge in bankruptcy at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Culver case, a -- a disciplinary case that we referred to in our brief, is a good illustration of this. Fraud turns on the defrauder's intent as a -- as a general matter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So if -- so if the lawyer said that, I can't give you advice in contemplation of bankruptcy, but I can tell you that fraud turns on the debtor's intent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the remedy for a violation of this is either an injunctive action by a government official, the U.S. trustee or by the Court or State attorney general, or actual damages paid to the debtor who has suffered harm from the unethical or abuse of advice given to him or her by the attorney."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So they have to -- for this one brother-in-law, they have to amend -- they're now violated the statute ex post facto somehow?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Milavetz, Gallop & Milavetz, P.A.",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF G. ERIC BRUNSTAD, JR. ON BEHALF OF MILAVETZ, GALLOP & MILAVETZ, P.A., ET AL."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the attorney, by saying, I take payment over time, and the debtor accepting that, the debtor would be incurring debt in contemplation of bankruptcy. Incurring debt to the attorney. The attorney would be proscribed, under the statute, from actually giving that particular advice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't read the hypothetical that you have given as coming within the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1deceb7b32f34de65523f5765746a7b04211f909484f55328ea073677c6749a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1deceb7b32f3-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
